thread:
Morgan: Quick UX sync — noticed a few issues in the compact composer when streaming is on. Token counter jumps, stop/regenerate controls get pushed off-screen on narrow view, and inserting from prompt library sometimes restarts the stream. Screenshot + short vid attached.
Alex: Can you drop the vid link? also, is the stop button supposed to be sticky? on desktop it feels fine but mobile is rough.
Morgan: https://files.internal/s/comp-composer-clip.mp4 — shows stop buried under the quick actions. Expected: stop stays visible and the token counter doesn't reflow mid-stream.
Jamie: Reflow makes it hard for keyboard users — focus moves unexpectedly when prompt library inserts. Suggest floating micro-toolbar for stop/regenerate + a reserved token meter slot in header.
Pat: From infra side: streaming emits partial tokens frequently; front-end currently re-renders token meter on every chunk. We could debounce updates (100–200ms) to smooth the counter. That'll also reduce layout thrash.
Aria: Accessibility nits: label buttons explicitly for screen readers (e.g., aria-label="Stop generation"). For streaming content, an aria-live="polite" region for the latest chunk helps screen-reader users follow output without focus jumps. Also confirm the floating toolbar is reachable via keyboard (tab order + visible focus ring).
Kevin: Small edge-case: when prompt library inserts, we mutate the composer DOM which triggers a full re-render; stream state isn't preserved so the server restarts generation. Would prefer to patch DOM only, or snapshot KV cache and reconnect without restarting the stream.
Alex: UX copy thought — 'Stop' vs 'Stop generation' — shorter is fine visually, but full phrase helps a11y. Maybe visible label = "Stop" and aria-label = "Stop generation"?
Jamie: Agree. Also accessibility: ensure the token counter has a numeric aria-live announcement when it crosses thresholds (e.g., 75%, 90%) so users know they're close to limits.
Morgan: Good call. Implementation plan idea: 1) floating micro-toolbar anchored to top-right of conversation frame on narrow widths, 2) reserve 48px height in header for token meter (prevents jump), 3) debounce meter updates to 150ms, 4) prompt library insertion does a minimal DOM patch + keeps stream session id.
Pat: I'll prototype the debounce + session-preserve change on the client; should be low risk. Backend already exposes session token for streaming.
design-bot: Preview build: https://playground.internal/pr-342 (mobile emulation included). Comments on the PR will have visual diffs.
Aria: Minor aria phrasing suggestion for token thresholds: announce "Token usage: 512 of 1024 tokens used (50%)" rather than just percentages. More actionable.
Kevin: On implementation, reserving header space means the composer needs to measure available height earlier — will add a CSS var + layout-safe area in JS. Example CSS we can use:
```css
.playground-header {
  --token-meter-height: 48px;
  padding-bottom: var(--token-meter-height);
}
.token-meter {
  height: var(--token-meter-height);
  position: absolute;
  right: 12px;
  top: 8px;
}
```
Jamie: Love the CSS approach — keeps layout stable. Also test with high-contrast and zoom 200% for a11y.
Morgan: Next steps: Jamie and Alex to finalize micro-toolbar placement & keyboard flow; Pat + Kevin to land debounce and session-preserve; Aria to write the a11y acceptance criteria; I'll merge after design-bot preview passes.
Alex: @Jamie want to pair on the mobile touch targets today? I'm free after standup. :thumbsup:
Jamie: Yep, ping me at 11:30. I'll bring test cases (keyboard nav, VoiceOver, TalkBack).
Morgan: Thanks team — logging this as a follow-up in the designer board.
